make_fcontext of boost.context on ARM before ARMv7 loads the address of its finish label from a
literal (ldr a2, =finish): an absolute R_ARM_ABS32 in .text, which lld refuses in a shared library
("cannot be used against local symbol; recompile with -fPIC") and ld.bfd turns into a text
relocation. adr, PC relative, is what ARMv7 uses and what the ARM state of every architecture has:
the literal stays for Thumb-1 only.

--- a/libs/context/src/asm/make_arm_aapcs_elf_gas.S
+++ b/libs/context/src/asm/make_arm_aapcs_elf_gas.S
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 
 
     @ compute abs address of label finish
-    #if __ARM_ARCH >= 7
+    #if __ARM_ARCH >= 7 || !defined(__thumb__)
     adr  a2, finish
     #else
     ldr  a2, =finish
